<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?>
<!--
    Calf rearing: what a hand-reared calf can eat at each age, in pens whose husbandry profile
    is marked rearing="true" (Hof Bergmann: the calf igloos and the calf rearing boxes A/B, see
    mod_support/FS25_HofBergmann/v1.5/husbandryProfiles.xml). Everywhere else calves keep the old
    rules, so a suckler calf with its mother in a barn or on pasture is not affected.

    Every hour each animal in a rearing pen may take at most milkMax x its food request from milk
    fill types and at most solidMax x its request from any other food (hay, TMR, silage...). The
    pen's trough is drawn down through the engine's own food consumption, with these caps; what
    the pen ate is then shared out by each animal's caps, so a weaned calf gets no milk even when
    a younger one drinks it beside it. The animal's food factor for health and growth is its own
    share x each fill type's productionWeight (animalFood.xml) over its request. A calf on solid
    feed alone before weaning, or on milk alone after it, is underfed and shows it.

    There is no calf starter fill type on the map. Solid feed is the map's cattle food; the
    calf pens' troughs take all of it (the map's avoidFillTypes is not read by the engine).

    Under the weight model v2 (weightProfiles.xml) calves are in the body condition budget from
    birth: each calf's own milk and solid liters are valued separately - milk at its fill type's
    energy (bodyCondition.xml feedEnergy, CALFMILK 1.20), solid feed at its energy x solidEnergy
    below - and the curves are read at the age within the month, so the change from milk to solid
    feed is gradual, with no step at weaning or at 6 months. Outside a rearing pen a calf's share
    of its pen's trough stands for its whole diet, suckling included, and is valued as any
    animal's: there is no milk to share out there. Without v2, calves under 6 months
    are outside the budget (bodyCondition.xml calfLegacyUntilAgeMonth) and an older animal still
    in a rearing pen keeps its own share there.

    enabled        Off: rearing pens feed like any pen.
    weaningMonth   Age (whole months) at which milk is being withdrawn. Housing moves at 2 months
                   (the igloo's maxAge="1"); this is a separate, later step.
    milkFillTypes  Fill types counted as milk.

    Curves: x = age - weaningMonth (months), y = share of the food request (linear between points,
    flat outside). With weaningMonth 3: 0-2 months PRE_WEANING, 3 WEANING, 4+ WEANED.
    milkMax    Most of the request that milk can cover.
    solidMax   Most of the request that solid feed can cover (rumen development).
    solidEnergy What a liter of solid feed is worth to the calf against a weaned animal (v2 only;
               must reach 1 after weaning). A design candidate, not a measured rumen curve.

    weaningMonth may be set per animalType, breed or subType below (same lookup as
    breedTraits.xml). Copy this file to modSettings/FS25_RealisticLivestockRM/calfRearing.xml to
    change it without editing the mod; an invalid file switches the feature off and logs why.
-->
<calfRearing enabled="true" weaningMonth="3" milkFillTypes="CALFMILK">
    <milkMax>
        <point x="-3" y="1.00"/>
        <point x="-2" y="0.90"/>
        <point x="-1" y="0.70"/>
        <point x="0" y="0.35"/>
        <point x="1" y="0.00"/>
    </milkMax>
    <solidMax>
        <point x="-3" y="0.10"/>
        <point x="-2" y="0.30"/>
        <point x="-1" y="0.60"/>
        <point x="0" y="0.90"/>
        <point x="1" y="1.00"/>
    </solidMax>
    <solidEnergy>
        <point x="-3" y="0.40"/>
        <point x="-2" y="0.55"/>
        <point x="-1" y="0.75"/>
        <point x="0" y="0.90"/>
        <point x="1" y="1.00"/>
    </solidEnergy>
</calfRearing>
